# trace_processor_shell's real stdout, captured verbatim (GRA-113/GRA-111).
# It writes CRLF line endings even on this Windows-hosted capture and must
# arrive at every reader exactly as it left the binary — parseRows() (in
# ../../perfetto.ts) is tested against these exact bytes, not against
# whatever a line-ending normalisation would leave behind. The root
# .gitattributes' `* text=auto eol=lf` would otherwise rewrite these to LF on
# checkout, which is a different byte stream than the one that produced them.
*.csv -text
